# The Sturmfels–Sullivant degree bound fails for ℤ/17 (machine-checked)

Main result: `SturmfelsSullivant.not_generatedInDegree_zmod17`, i.e. the ideal of the group-based
model for `ℤ/17` on the claw tree `K_{1,3}` is NOT generated in degree `≤ 17` (combinatorial form of
Michałek, arXiv:1508.04177, Section 2).  Hence [SS05, Conjecture 29] is false.

First part (`namespace Z17`): core counting lemma on pairs.

Counterexample: G. Pochuev, 8 September 2026
(https://github.com/Grisha-Pochuev/phylogenetic-complexity-z17-counterexample).
Flows on three leaves over ℤ/17 are encoded by their first two entries; the third is `-a - b`.
`PA`, `PB` are the two 18-row tables.  `fibre_eq` shows that a multiset of pairs with the same three
column multisets as `PA` is `PA` or `PB`.

Proof: every row lies in the list `T` of 22 admissible pairs (finite check); the column conditions
give 23 linear equations in the 22 multiplicities; these force the multiplicity vector to be that
of `PA` or of `PB` (linear integer arithmetic).  This file is partly generated by `gen_core.py`.
-/
